<title>INDIA: India's RBI sets repo cut-off at 4.05 percent.</title>
<headline>India's RBI sets repo cut-off at 4.05 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it set a cut-off interest rate of 4.05 percent at Thursday's four-day repo auction.</p>
<p>The cut-off at the earlier auction on Monday was 4.15 percent.  </p>
<p>The RBI said it received 14 bids for 46.75 billion rupees of which it accepted 11 for 45.50 billion rupees.</p>
<p>The weighted average cut-off rate was 3.9960 percent.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
